# Build assets are real files, and a request for one that does not exist must
# fail as a 404. Without this rule the SPA fallback below answers it with
# index.html and a 200 instead.
#
# That is not hypothetical. On the 20 Aug deploy a request for
# /assets/index-CllsAgWs.css arrived while the deployment was still propagating,
# the fallback answered it with the HTML shell and a 200, and the /assets/* rule
# in _headers stamped that HTML `immutable, max-age=31536000`. Cloudflare cached
# an HTML document under a .css URL, `nosniff` correctly refused to apply it as a
# stylesheet, and the entire app rendered unstyled — with a 200, no console
# error, and a year to live. A transient 404 became a permanent success.
#
# Ordering matters: first match wins, so this has to sit above the catch-all.
# Static files are matched before _redirects is consulted, so this rule only
# ever fires for an asset that genuinely is not there.
/assets/*  /404.html  404

# SPA fallback.
#
# Routing is client-side (react-router), so the server has no /today, /map or
# /visit/:id to serve. Without this, a rep who bookmarks a screen — or reloads
# mid-visit — gets a 404 instead of the app.
/*  /index.html  200
